<title>SOUTH KOREA: Sammi Corp has 170 bln won in outstanding bonds.</title>
<headline>Sammi Corp has 170 bln won in outstanding bonds.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sammi Corp had 170 billion won worth of outstanding corporate and convertible bond issues, the Securities Supervisory Board said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Sammi Corp, a trading arm of Sammi Steel Co, has filed for court receivership.  </p>
<p>The stock market watchdog said in a statement Sammi Corp had 84 billion won worth of outstanding corporate bonds and 86 billion won worth of outstanding convertible bonds.</p>
<p>An official at the board said if Sammi Corp was granted court receivership, its payment on all debts, including bonds, would be frozen.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
